# M7 - e2e test gate for the swarm simulation (DONE)

## Final merge resolution (manus-parity 8270c75 -> khamis1992/mf2-m7)
The gate failed on the mandatory pre-step: `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity`.
`manus-parity` had advanced (tip `8270c75`, carrying the M2 seed and M5 intent work)
past the earlier merge (`a32783a`), so `git merge manus-parity` re-conflicted.

Topology (verified, not assumed):
- `merge-base HEAD MERGE_HEAD` = `74d0d09` (the manus-parity tip the earlier merge used).
- `8270c75` is NOT an ancestor of `a32783a`: it is the newer manus-parity tip and
  brings `src/tools/mirofish/intent.ts`, `locale.ts`, `model.ts`, `seed.ts` and the
  `settings.ts` location setting.
- `74d0d09` has only `src/tools/mirofish.ts`; HEAD (`a45e8ba`) has the M7 files
  (`pipeline.ts`, `types.ts`, `__tests__/`).

Conflicts resolved keeping BOTH sides:
- `src/tools/mirofish/types.ts` - the M2 seed/locale/persona types and the M7
  pipeline/report types describe the same domain objects. Merged into one supertype
  file: `LocaleProfile`, `IncomeBand`, `Persona` and `SimulationSettings` are defined
  once and satisfy both consumers. `Persona` keeps every seed field (`bio`,
  `nationality`, `incomeAmount`, `household`, `channel`, `attitude`, `habits`,
  `occupation`, `diet`) alongside the M7 aliases (`profession`, `interestedTopics`,
  `mbti`), with the M2-only fields optional so neither stage is weakened.
  `MirofishPipelineUnavailableError`, `SeedResult` and the `SeedModelCaller` re-export
  are all retained.
- `src/tools/mirofish.ts` - kept the M5 intent routing (`classifyWithSession`,
  `extractMirofishSettings`, the `location` session field) and the M7 tool contract.
- `src/server/settings.ts` - kept the new `location` setting (validate on load and on
  update, drop malformed values) that M2/M5 introduced.

Also restored: `.jdone` had been staged as deleted by the earlier resolution even
though all three merge parents (`74d0d09`, `8270c75`, `a32783a`) carry the same blob
`b2a9e94`. Restored to HEAD so the marker is no longer dropped.

## Static gate defect found and fixed
The static check was DEAD CODE: it sat behind the same `{ skip: !ready }` capability
guard as the pipeline scenarios, so it never ran while the stages were un-built, and it
only scanned the new pipeline modules - which do not import the legacy fake code.
Fix:
- `staticGateTargets()` now also scans `src/tools/mirofish.ts` (the `mirofish_chat`
  tool) and the `/api/mirofish/*` region of `src/server/http.ts`, so the scan can
  actually see the fake implementation.
- Added an always-runs self-check, "static gate detects the legacy fake
  implementation", which replays a snippet of the original fake implementation
  through the same patterns and asserts every pattern is caught. It also asserts the
  self-check fixture exercises every pattern, so a real detection cannot regress
  silently.
- The scan itself stays capability-guarded (`skip: !ready`): the legacy fake tool
  still emits fake personas and hard-coded result numbers today, so the assertion is
  EXPECTED to fail there. It turns on automatically when a stage task flips the flag,
  where failing on the leftover fake code is the intended signal.

False-positive scoping: the earlier `readdirSync` and bare-percentage patterns were
too broad - they matched legitimate filesystem reads (`src/server/http.ts` 1279/2139/
2214) and legitimate prose percentages (SLA uptime, "10x", coverage notes). Replaced
with patterns anchored on shapes a real simulation cannot produce: a persona named
after a job title, a literal `75%` inside a result template, and `approval_rate_*`
keys. `http.ts` is scanned only within the `/api/mirofish/*` routes.

### Router scope (second pass, commit 8701d2f)
The shared router is a single ~2800-line file that also serves hundreds of unrelated
routes, so scanning it wholesale would make the gate report noise (or hide real hits
behind it). The first version used a fixed 90-line window, which was arbitrary and
could drift away from the routes. Replaced with `inScopeLines()`, which marks a
route's own line plus its handler body and ends at the next blank line (the router
separates every handler with one). Brace counting was tried first and rejected: the
route's own `if (...)` line contains the route string inside quotes, and template
literals inside a handler distort the depth, so the region closed early and
excluded the very handler it was meant to cover.

The always-on self-check now asserts the scope invariant directly: every
`/api/mirofish/*` route line is in scope, and the scoped region stays small relative
to the whole router. A refactor that moved or renamed the routes would otherwise
shrink the scanned region to nothing while the gate still reported green. This
assertion caught two real bugs in the first attempt (an indentation-only terminator
that closed on the handler's object argument, and a `path.join` comparison that
never matched an absolute path on Windows).

## What M7 ships (commit ca4411f)
- `src/tools/mirofish/types.ts` - public pipeline contract: `ModelCaller` (injectable,
  the only model boundary), `LocaleProfile`, `Persona`, `SimulationEvent`,
  `RoundMetrics`, `SwarmReport`, `PipelineResult`, `MirofishChatRequest`,
  `MirofishPipelineUnavailableError`.
- `src/tools/mirofish/pipeline.ts` - `runMirofishPipeline` (seed -> simulate ->
  report) and `runMirofishChat` (the entry point shared with the `mirofish_chat`
  tool), plus the per-stage capability check `mirofishPipelineReady()`.
- `src/tools/mirofish/__tests__/nutrio-e2e.test.ts` - the e2e gate. A deterministic
  fake `ModelCaller` whose replies depend on prompt content (locale keywords drive
  currency/dialect; the active price drives purchase intent), so price and location
  genuinely change outcomes. Four scenarios:
  1. Doha/QAR/Arabic-Gulf: report mentions Nutrio, keto and both prices; personas use QAR.
  2. Price sensitivity 1200 / 1450 / 99999 -> three distinct purchase-intent metrics.
  3. Location: London -> GBP/English and a report that differs from Doha; unset
     location -> inferred from the brief.
  4. Static gate: scans the MiroFish sources for hard-coded result numbers, fake
     personas (`Developer`/`SecurityAuditor`/...), fake agent roles and
     `approval_rate_*` keys, and fails if any are found.
- `src/tools/mirofish/__tests__/fixtures/nutrio-briefs.ts` - Nutrio / نتريو meal
  subscription brief (price QAR 1200 -> 1450, new keto plan) with Doha, London and
  unset-location variants plus `withPrice`.
- `package.json` - added `"test:mirofish"`.

## Capability guard (per the task spec)
The pipeline stages (seed/simulate/report) are not implemented on manus-parity, so
`mirofishPipelineReady()` returns false and every scenario skips via `skip: !ready`
(no `test.todo`). The suite prints which checks are pending and stays green. A later
stage task flips its own capability flag in `pipeline.ts` and the matching assertions
turn on automatically. The static scanner itself is covered by the always-on
self-check, so the gate is never dead code while skipped.

