# J8 - Cross-session file-touch notifications: DONE

## What J8 delivers

jcode notifies a session when another session writes a file it has already read,
so a stale read is caught instead of silently producing a conflicting edit. Loam
runs several agent sessions against one repository (sub-agents, delegated tasks,
orchestrator workers, swarm stages), so the port is a per-workspace notice queue
shared by every live session against that root.

Spec: `ref/SWARM_ARCHITECTURE.md` "File Touch and Intent" and `ref/JCODE_RE.md`
task J8. Ported to TypeScript; jcode's notice semantics are kept.

## What was added

- `src/tools/fileTouch.ts` (new, 353 lines): `FileTouchRegistry` with
  `noteRead` / `noteWrite` / `noteDelete` / `drainNotices` / `forgetSession`;
  `fileTouchRegistry(workspace)` returns one registry per repository root;
  `forgetFileTouchSession(sessionId)` drops a finished session's marks.
  Notices are deduped per (session, path) so repeated edits update one pending
  notice instead of flooding the reader. A writer never notifies itself, a write
  that changes nothing produces no notice, and a reader who re-read the file
  after the edit is not told about it. `diffLines` is an LCS line diff with a
  multiset fallback above 300 lines (where the quadratic table would cost more
  than the notice is worth); `formatDiffSummary` renders `+2/-1` and
  `formatDiffPreview` returns up to 3 changed lines prefixed `-`/`+`. Content is
  identified by SHA-256, not a short rolling hash, because "same digest" is
  treated as "the reader already holds this content" and a collision would
  silently suppress a real change. Bounded throughout: 50 pending notices per
  session, 5000 tracked paths, 50 live registries, a 1-hour pending TTL, and a
  256k cap above which a reader's snapshot is kept as a digest only.
- `src/tools/readState.ts`: `ReadTouchHooks` (`read` / `write` / `remove`) fired
  by `record` / `recordWrite` / `forget`, so read tracking publishes to the
  registry. Also `recent(limit)` with a `readAtMs` timestamp.
- `src/agent/loop.ts`: one registry per workspace root, the `readState.hooks`
  wiring, `touch.drainNotices(sessionId)` into the reminder channel at each
  turn, `forgetFileTouchSession` when a session ends, and a `subSeq` per-subagent
  session id so a child is a distinct session.
- `src/agent/reminders.ts`: `fileTouchedReminder` plus `ReminderChannel.fileTouched`,
  delivered as a hidden user-role block that the UI cannot render.
- Write-side publishing: `src/tools/files.ts` (`recordWrite` on write,
  `forget` + `recordWrite` on `file_move`, `forget` on `file_delete`),
  `src/tools/multiEdit.ts`, `src/tools/subagents.ts`, `src/tools/wideResearch.ts`,
  `src/tools/mapReduce.ts`, `src/swarm/service.ts`,
  `src/subagent/inProcessProvider.ts`, `src/subagent/types.ts`.
- `packages/web/public/marketplace/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`: jcode (MIT) attribution
  for the file-touch feature.

The follow-up fix `b02e220` closed two defects: notices for snapshots too large
to retain (the digest-only path) and digest collisions.

## Acceptance criteria (automated, all passing)

| Requirement | Test |
| --- | --- |
| session B is told when session A writes a file B read | `fileTouch.test.ts` "notifies a reader when another session writes a file it read" |
| no notice for a file the session never read | "sends no notice for a file nobody read" |
| a writer is never notified of its own write | "never notifies the writer about its own write" |
| an unchanged write produces no notice | "sends no notice when the write changes nothing" |
| a reader who re-read after the edit is not told | "does not notify a reader who re-read the file after the edit" |
| repeated edits collapse into one pending notice | "collapses repeated edits to one path into a single pending notice" |
| every reader is told, the writer is not | "notifies every reader but not the writer" |
| readers are told about a delete | "tells readers when a file is deleted" |
| a finished session's queue and marks are dropped | "forgets a finished session's queue and reader marks" |
| the per-session queue is bounded | "keeps the per-session queue bounded" |
| a reader whose snapshot was too large is still told | "notifies a reader whose snapshot was too large to retain" |
| line diff summary and preview | `diffLines` "reports added and removed lines and keeps a short preview" |
| identical content is no change | "treats identical content as no change" |
| large files use the multiset fallback | "falls back to a multiset count for very large files" |
| the digest does not collide across files | "does not treat two different files as identical (digest has no collisions)" |
| notices reach the agent loop | `fileTouchLoop.test.ts` "file-touch notices in the agent loop" (3 tests) |
| read-tracking guard still holds (NOT_READ / STALE) | `readState.test.ts` "read-tracking guard" (9 tests) |
| read / write / remove hooks publish the content each saw | "publishes read, write, and remove with the content each one saw" |
| a moved file is forgotten and republished at the new path | "forgets a moved file and publishes the new path as a write" |
| the notice is injected as a hidden reminder | `reminders.test.ts` file-touch block (13 tests in the suite) |

