(`grep took 1278ms`, threshold 1000ms). This is a wall-clock timing assertion, not a logic
failure: the machine had 709 processes running under the live parity runner. Evidence it is not a
regression: the file and its implementation are byte-identical to `3136f14` (empty
`git diff 3136f14 HEAD` for `search.test.ts`, `search.ts`, `glob.ts`, `grep.ts`), it passes 5/5
in isolation, and the immediately following full run passed 2940/2940. No test was edited.

