# N9 round 11: parity re-tracked .jdone, so the earlier merge silently dropped this report

## What happened, and why the previous tip was not actually done

The previous tip `76906c0` merged `manus-parity` at `9ffdb16`. Parity had re-added `.jdone` to
its tree, while this branch still matched `.jdone` in `.gitignore:50`. A gitignore entry does
**not** stop a merge that brings a tracked path in from the other side, and git did not warn:
the untracked working-tree `.jdone` (which held this report) was replaced by parity's rollup
with no conflict, no error, and no entry in `git status`. The N9 report was silently dropped.
Detected by re-checking instead of trusting the green merge: `git ls-tree HEAD -- .jdone` was
non-empty while the N9 heading was absent from both the working tree and `HEAD:.jdone`.

Fix: the report was restored and committed at `c98f3bf` as a tracked file, so the marker exists
both on disk and at HEAD.

## Merge round 11 (this session)

Parity advanced again to `495ac5f` (39 commits: cr-04, N10, N7, V8, `.gitattributes` union rule,
`src/agent/prompt.ts`, `src/config.ts`, `src/design/registry.ts` + `retrieval.ts`, `src/index.ts`,
`src/server/runTools.ts` + its test, `src/tools/uiExamples.ts` + its test).

`.jdone` conflicted. Resolved with git's own union driver (`git merge-file --union`), which is
exactly the semantics parity adopted in `.gitattributes` (`.jdone merge=union`, `.jcode-done
merge=union`). Verified as a strict multiset: **0 lines under-present from either side**
(ours 3494 distinct, theirs 5075 distinct), no conflict markers, no BOM, no U+FFFD. My N9 report
and parity's V8 round-12 report are both intact.

Parity's only test change in this merge is `src/server/__tests__/runTools.test.ts`, which is
**additive only (2 insertions, 0 deletions)**: it registers the real `ui_examples` tool so the
always-on tool list matches the shipped registry. No assertion removed, relaxed, or skipped. No
test was weakened by this task.

