# N9 done: ask-user clarification node

## What shipped (already merged upstream before this session)

The N9 implementation is intact in the tree and was not re-implemented:

- `src/tools/askUserStore.ts` - in-memory pending-request records with a TTL.
- `src/tools/askUserGate.ts` - the `ask_user` payload type/parsing plus the two classifiers
  (pending-request tool-call blocker, vague-prompt auto-trigger).
- `src/tools/askUserTools.ts` - the `ask_user` agent tool (questions with options, free-text
  answers, an uploaded file) and `applyAskUserGate`, which wraps every mutating tool.
- `src/server/routes/askUser.ts` - the HTTP route the web client answers through.
- `packages/web/src/components/approval/AskUserCard.tsx` - the chat-event card, localized
  (Arabic included) with logical CSS properties.
- Registered in the tool registry (`src/index.ts`) and the mode-catalog CONTROL set
  (`src/modes/catalog.ts`); wording in `src/agent/prompt.ts` and the web i18n catalogs.
- `packages/shared/src/socket.ts` carries the `askUserRequested` / `askUserResolved` shapes.

## What this session changed

No source file was edited and no test was weakened. This session fixed the gate failures, which
were merge conflicts in the tracked rollup `.jdone`, and then kept merging an advancing
`manus-parity` under a live runner:

1. `f14c3d1` merge manus-parity (bdae2ca, J11 round 9): resolved `.jdone` keeping both sides.
2. `14e04b3` merge manus-parity (84c9af8, N3): resolved `.jdone` keeping both sides.
3. `2d99ac8` recorded the session in the rollup.
4. `085cfb5` merge manus-parity (d3d7b88): parity untracked `.jdone`/`.jcode-done`
   ("chore: untrack runner markers .jdone/.jcode-done ... caused .jdone merge conflicts"), so the
   modify/delete conflict was resolved by deleting the local copies to match upstream.
5. `f923e19` merge manus-parity (bec4181, packaging 0.5.29): clean, no conflict.
6. `41890e1` merge manus-parity (cde859f, memory subsystem): clean, no conflict.
