    below** - parity re-tracked `.jdone` and the merge silently replaced the working-tree copy.

## Defect found and fixed by independent validation (not by the gate runner)

`9ffdb16` re-added `.jdone` to the parity tree (`git ls-tree manus-parity -- .jdone` is
`100644 blob`), while this branch still matched it in `.gitignore:50`. A gitignore entry does
**not** stop a merge that brings a tracked path in from the other side, and git did not warn:
the untracked working-tree `.jdone` (which held this report) was overwritten by parity's rollup
with no conflict, no error and no entry in `git status`. The N9 report was silently dropped.

Detected by re-checking rather than trusting the green merge: `git ls-tree HEAD -- .jdone` was
non-empty while `git status` stayed clean, and the N9 heading was absent from both the working
tree and `HEAD:.jdone`. Fix: the report is restored below, prepended to the tracked rollup and
committed, so the marker is both present on disk and tracked at HEAD.

## Acceptance criteria (automated, passing)

1. Vague prompt fixture -> ask node appears before any tool call:
   `src/agent/__tests__/askUserAutoTrigger.test.ts` passes. A vague prompt emits
   `ask_user_required` and the planner is never called while the card waits; the classifier block
   sits before `planTask`, so no agent loop and no tool call can run first.
2. Answer + file -> run resumes and uses the file:
   `src/tools/__tests__/askUser.test.ts` and `src/protocol/__tests__/askUserSocket.test.ts` pass,
   including the uploaded-file resume case. The card component is covered by vitest +
   @testing-library (`askUserCard.test.tsx`, 7 tests); Playwright was not used.

