## M3 gate-fix session (round 7): re-merged parity N19/F6 (`ca08d4c`); the union driver auto-resolved `.jdone` with no conflict

`.jgatefail.txt` reported: `MERGE CONFLICT with latest manus-parity in: .jdone. Run
git merge manus-parity, resolve those files keeping both sides, commit.`

### Root cause
No source file conflicted. The only conflict path is the tracked rollup `.jdone`, because both
sides append their own completion report at the same anchor.

### What happened this round
Parity advanced again, from the round-6 tip `495ac5f` (V8) to `ca08d4c` (`merge
khamis1992/neo-n19 (N19 via loam-jcode-run) into manus-parity`, carrying the F6 video-export
workstream). `git merge manus-parity` **completed with exit 0 and no conflict**: `.jdone` was
auto-merged by the committed `.gitattributes` union driver (`Auto-merging .jdone`), and no
source file needed a manual resolve. This is the root-cause fix working as designed: the
recurring gate failure cannot recur now that the union rule is present.

The union driver concatenated both sides. Verified mechanically against both parents
(multiset diff of non-blank lines): 0 lines missing from parent 1 (`5d0a29d`) and 0 lines
missing from parent 2 (`ca08d4c`), so the result is a strict superset and no report content
was dropped.

### Integrity of the merge
- `.jdone` blob `a95b3b0` at the parity tip is present verbatim; this branch's round-5/6
  reports stay at the top and parity's N19/F6 rollup is appended below.
- 0 conflict markers remain in any tracked file (`^(<{7}|={7}|>{7}|\|{7})$` matches zero lines).
- LF-only working copy, valid UTF-8, no BOM, no NUL/U+FFFD, Arabic intact.
- No mirofish file changed in this merge (`git diff --name-only 495ac5f ca08d4c --
  src/tools/mirofish` is empty), so the M3 deliverable is untouched.
- No forbidden path staged: `docs/handoff/watchdog.ps1`, `qa/*.png`,
  `packages/tests/visual/baselines`, and ZCode/Codex files are untouched.
- No test was weakened, deleted or skipped. No secret committed. No force-push, no `reset --hard`.

### The M3 deliverable (unchanged this round, committed at `6bcbe4c`)
`fix(mirofish): record sharedWith[] share provenance in the M3 turn schema` adds the
`sharedWith` field to the agent-turn output schema so share provenance (who the agent
amplified or answered) is recorded: the `AgentTurnOutput.sharedWith: string[]` type, the
`MAX_SHARED_WITH = 8` cap, validation that accepts `sharedWith` / `shared_with` /
`sharedAgents`, the field in the two neutral fallbacks, and the model prompt rule and JSON
example. Covered by `src/tools/mirofish/__tests__/simulate.test.ts`.

### Gates (all run from the worktree root on the final merged tree `9f67341`)
- `git merge-base --is-ancestor manus-parity HEAD`               -> exit 0 (0 commits missing)
- `git rev-list --left-right --count manus-parity...HEAD`       -> 0 (parity fully merged)
- `npx tsc --noEmit`                                             -> exit 0
- `npm run build:server`                                         -> exit 0
- `npm run check:encoding`                                       -> exit 0 (no BOM, no mojibake)
- `npm run verify`                                               -> exit 0
    (typecheck + check:encoding + check:eval + orchestrator 114/114 + check:recovery +
     check:modes; "orchestrator smoke: PASS (114/114)")
- `(cd packages/web && npx next build)`                          -> exit 0 (25/25 static pages)
- `node --import tsx --test src/tools/mirofish/__tests__/*.test.ts
   src/agent/__tests__/mirofishLoop.test.ts src/server/__tests__/mirofishHttp.test.ts
   src/tools/__tests__/mirofishIntent.test.ts`                     -> exit 0 (144 tests, 144 pass)
- `(cd packages/web && npx vitest run)`                          -> exit 0 (91 files, 624 tests)

Note on vitest: the first full run failed once in the pre-existing flaky
`packages/web/src/app/app/wiki/__tests__/wikiPage.test.tsx` ("opens a page through GET
/api/wiki/:project/:slug"). It passes in isolation (2/2) and passes on a full re-run
